Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 20:12:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] voxtral tts: cover per-request noise seeding and euler
 steps

Pins the three properties the feature exists for: an unseeded batch stays
bit-for-bit upstream, a seed reproduces its own frame sequence, and a seeded
row is unaffected by who shares its batch (the property a global-RNG approach
cannot have). Plus the guards: batch/row mismatch refuses rather than seeding
the wrong request, and euler_steps needs batch agreement.

The class is instantiated via __new__ + nn.Module.__init__ because the real
__init__ wants a VllmConfig and the checkpoint, while both methods under test
only read n_acoustic_codebook.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
